module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.probe_manifest_overwrites_emitted_dependency_demand

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data probe_manifest_overwrites_emitted_dependency_demand: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "probe_manifest_overwrites_emitted_dependency_demand" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: the emitter derives Cargo dependency demand from the emitted program, then the native probe writer replaces Cargo.toml with the stage0 foundation dependency roster. The two producers answer different questions while naming one artifact.",
    "RECEIPT: native-filesystem-fold at 5c3d566a768 emitted 185 files for the native CLI, including an async service driver. The assembled native crate refused with E0433 for tokio and E0752 for async main. The focused native controls built against the original emitted manifest and passed; their green did not establish the assembled route.",
    "REPAIR: emitted_closure_compile_host consumes the unique emitted Cargo.toml and preserves its dependency and feature tables. It changes only the per-entry package name and carries the original library name so generated main.rs can still address the emitted crate.",
    "CONTROL (historical, deleted with the adapter it tested): manifest_preserves_emitted_dependency_demand passed both synchronous and asynchronous manifests from emit_cargo_toml through probe_manifest. Its successor is the_clap_dependency_follows_the_emitted_cli_demand_in_both_directions over v1.compiler.stage0_crates emitted_crate_dependencies, and the workspace writer refuses an emission naming zero or several Rust crates rather than supplying a roster.",
    "CEILING: the host still adapts package identity through TOML. This construction removes its second dependency authority; it does not prove that the emitter has modeled every dependency demand correctly. The native emit/build/fault/restore route remains the executed discriminator for that larger claim.",
    "RECEIPT (second route, same class): gunbc#12861 made the emitted v1_rt read the thread CPU clock through libc and added libc to the emitter, the stage0 crates and two hand-authored .dag transport manifests. A third hand copy, the curated seed-linked harness dependency block, was missed, and every module on the behavioral transport roster builds through it: fleet run 37079504327 returned 15 of 15 rows with no verdict on E0433 for libc. //gunbc/instruments:self-host does not build through that block and stayed green. The first repair had closed the Rust probe writer only; the .dag harness routes carried the same overwrite.",
    "REPAIR (second route): tools.emitted_crate_harness_manifest derive_harness_manifest_in_place reads the Cargo.toml the emission wrote and appends only what the harness owns -- its [lib] and [[bin]] target tables and, for a seed-linked build, the v1-compiler path dependency as its own subtable. The curated harness, the emission entry instrument, the product receipt stage and both std.logic transports consume it; their hand-authored dependency blocks are deleted, and no .dag harness route names a registry crate. An absent emitted manifest refuses rather than falling back to a roster.",
    "THIRD REPAIR (structural): the emission no longer renders a Cargo.toml at all. v1.compiler.emit_rust returns its crate facts (gunbc.rust_emitted_crate EmittedRustCrate: crate name and dependency demand), and every emitted-Rust route -- the probe crate writer, gunbc compile --target rust, the native lane -- writes the partitioned workspace through cli_run::emitted_crate_workspace_host write_emitted_workspace, whose manifests v1.compiler.stage0_crates renders with the demand's registry dependencies. probe_manifest and emit_cargo_toml are deleted, so the Rust probe writer has no manifest to overwrite or adapt. The .dag harness routes still append their own tables to the root package's manifest.",
    "CONTROL (second route): test.claim.emitted_crate_harness_manifest_witness supplies an emitted manifest carrying a dependency no harness names and requires it in the derived manifest for every target and linkage, requires the seed dependency table exactly when the build is seed-linked, and requires a refusal when the emitted manifest was not read or is empty. The inhabitance claim for the real emitter is the behavioral transport roster itself: its rows build through the derived manifest.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
